## Facts & Assumptions

**Given:** Full AC, a locally flat proper slice disk $D$, a connected oriented Seifert surface $F$ for $\partial D$, and matching boundary collars.

[A1] Full AC is the family-of-nonempty-sets choice axiom. [[def-axiom-of-choice]]

[F1] A locally flat proper surface has explicit interior and boundary pair charts and a product collar at its boundary. [[def-locally-flat-proper-surface-and-concordance-collars]]

[F2] Alexander duality gives the first homology of the complement of the compact locally contractible capped surface as $\mathbb Z$, generated by a meridian. [[thm-alexander-duality-for-compact-locally-contractible-subsets-of-a-sphere]]

## Proof

1.1 Under the stated local-flatness hypothesis, [F1] supplies the pair charts and boundary collar for $D$ and the product-collar data needed to form the capped surface. This records the available local geometry, but it does not construct the asserted embedded $3$-manifold. [A1, F1, given, construct]

1.2 [F2] determines the complement's meridian homology class, but that homology calculation alone does not construct a map with a locally flat regular fiber or an oriented bicollar. Livingston's cited regular-value argument is for a smooth disk and does not establish this locally flat statement. No proof of the claimed $R$ is supplied here; the item remains escalated. [F2, step 1.1, given, construct]

