The smooth-disk construction in Livingston's proof of Theorem 2.6 uses a smooth map on $B^4\setminus D$ and a regular-value argument. The present Statement includes a locally flat topological disk. I have not completed the required locally flat Seifert-hypersurface construction for that category, including a justified locally flat regular fiber and its collar at $D$. The cited source's short argument does not supply that topological-category proof. This item remains escalated; do not use [F2] alone as proof of the asserted embedded three-manifold.
